ion/vite` path\nhas the broadest Fronts fixture. `vite-plugin-federation` is verified through its MF2 manifest.\nOriginJS is intentionally a narrower, production-only ESM `remoteEntry.js` compatibility path."},"10":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started-8","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started#define-an-application","content":"React and Vue producers use `defineReactApp()` and `defineVueApp()` but export the same branded\napplication contract."},"11":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started-9","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started#compose-a-local-host","content":"Use this same Host transaction in a shell, producer development page, Storybook, or integration\ntest. There is no separate global registration or standalone lifecycle API."},"12":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started-10","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started#add-module-federation-delivery","content":"Create an explicit official Runtime instance and pass it to `@fronts/mf`. The adapter maps one\nresolved deployment to public `registerRemotes()`, `preloadRemote()`, and `loadRemote()` calls. It\ndoes not own manifests or the share graph."},"13":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started-11","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started#add-module-federation-delivery","content":"Continue with the Host Runtime API for cancellation,\nresolution-aware containers, contextual services, replacement, audit, and shutdown. Read\nModule Federation integrations before claiming producer\ncompatibility."},"14":{"id":"/en/docs/getting-started-12","page_id":"/en/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/getting-started#verify-a-repository-checkout","content":"The non-browser gate builds and packs every public package, imports tarballs through ESM and\nCommonJS, typechecks the workspace, and enforces coverage. The two browser modes prove development\ncomposition and fresh production output."},"15":{"id":"/en/docs","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"page","content":"Fronts 2.0 Documentation","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs"},"16":{"id":"/en/docs-0","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Learn the framework-neutral application contract, Host Runtime, delivery integrations, isolation boundaries, operations, and release policy."},"17":{"id":"/en/docs-1","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Choose the right layer"},"18":{"id":"/en/docs-2","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs#recommended-reading-path","content":"Recommended reading path"},"19":{"id":"/en/docs-3","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs#what-the-repository-proves","content":"What the repository proves"},"20":{"id":"/en/docs-4","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs#documentation-sources","content":"Documentation sources"},"21":{"id":"/en/docs-5","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Fronts is a framework-neutral **application runtime** for independently delivered web applications.\nIt starts where a module loader stops: after code can be discovered, a platform still needs a stable\napplication ABI, trusted identity, lifecycle ownership, deployment policy, isolation, scoped host\ncapabilities, readiness, replacement, cancellation, observability, and cleanup."},"22":{"id":"/en/docs-6","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Fronts 2.0 is implemented and tested but has not yet been published to npm. Public APIs and\nprotocols may still change before the first stable release."},"23":{"id":"/en/docs-7","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Need"},"24":{"id":"/en/docs-8","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Use"},"25":{"id":"/en/docs-9","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Load an MF remote or use an official React/Vue Bridge"},"26":{"id":"/en/docs-10","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Module Federation Runtime or Bridge directly"},"27":{"id":"/en/docs-11","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Run a Fronts application without Module Federation"},"28":{"id":"/en/docs-12","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"`@fronts/core` with any application loader"},"29":{"id":"/en/docs-13","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Load a Fronts application through MF Runtime"},"30":{"id":"/en/docs-14","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"`@fronts/core`, `@fronts/mf`, and `@module-federation/runtime`"},"31":{"id":"/en/docs-15","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Build an MF producer"},"32":{"id":"/en/docs-16","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"A supported producer plugin such as the official Vite or Rsbuild integration"},"33":{"id":"/en/docs-17","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Govern apps across frameworks, loaders, isolation levels, and release policy"},"34":{"id":"/en/docs-18","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"A Fronts Host"},"35":{"id":"/en/docs-19","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#choose-the-right-layer","content":"Fronts deliberately does not parse MF manifests, choose shared dependencies, mutate snapshots, or\nreplace bundler plugins. Those remain Module Federation responsibilities."},"36":{"id":"/en/docs-20","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#recommended-reading-path","content":"Quick start — define and mount one application."},"37":{"id":"/en/docs-21","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#recommended-reading-path","content":"Decision record — understand why Fronts remains useful after MF 2."},"38":{"id":"/en/docs-22","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#recommended-reading-path","content":"Architecture — learn layers and ownership boundaries."},"39":{"id":"/en/docs-23","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#recommended-reading-path","content":"Application contract — learn the producer ABI."},"40":{"id":"/en/docs-24","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#recommended-reading-path","content":"Host Runtime API — compose and operate a Host."},"41":{"id":"/en/docs-25","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#recommended-reading-path","content":"Module Federation integrations — choose a verified delivery path."},"42":{"id":"/en/docs-26","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#what-the-repository-proves","content":"The repository verifies the core-only lifecycle, real official MF Runtime loading, React and Vue\nproducers, DOM and Shadow DOM targets, a cross-origin iframe agent, readiness-gated replacement,\ncontextual capability services, and compatible Vite producers. Development-server and fresh\nproduction-preview browser suites exercise the same application contract."},"43":{"id":"/en/docs-27","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#what-the-repository-proves","content":"Use the support policy to distinguish declared, CI-verified,\nfixture-verified, best-effort, and unsupported combinations."},"44":{"id":"/en/docs-28","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#documentation-sources","content":"The English technical pages are generated from the repository's canonical Markdown and package\nREADMEs. Chinese pages use the same slug inventory and are validated as a complete parallel tree.\nExact TypeScript signatures and package ranges remain authoritative in source code and package\nmanifests; this site explains intent, boundaries, workflows, and verification."},"45":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"page","content":"Application Contract","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Core concepts","Core concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract"},"46":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-0","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","content":"Framework-neutral application protocol, lifecycle ownership, readiness, services, and compatibility rules for Fronts 2.0."},"47":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-1","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#protocol-identity","content":"Protocol identity"},"48":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-2","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"Mount input"},"49":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-3","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-output","content":"Mount output"},"50":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-4","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#ready","content":"`ready`"},"51":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-5","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#updateprops","content":"`update(props)`"},"52":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-6","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#activate-and-deactivate","content":"`activate()` and `deactivate()`"},"53":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-7","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#unmount","content":"`unmount()`"},"54":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-8","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#state-machine","content":"State machine"},"55":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-9","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#cancellation","content":"Cancellation"},"56":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-10","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"Capabilities"},"57":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-11","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#framework-adapters","content":"Framework adapters"},"58":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-12","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#react","content":"React"},"59":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-13","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#vue-3","content":"Vue 3"},"60":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-14","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#compatibility-rule","content":"Compatibility rule"},"61":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-15","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#verification","content":"Verification"},"62":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-16","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#protocol-identity","content":"Every producer exports a `FrontsApp` created by `defineApp()`, `defineReactApp()`, or\n`defineVueApp()`. The helper adds a non-enumerable symbol brand plus enumerable protocol name and\nversion fields. The symbol is a local marker; the cross-package ABI is the structural mount shape\nplus the protocol name and major version. The host validates that ABI, and a symbol brand never\nbypasses protocol-version validation."},"63":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-17","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#protocol-identity","content":"The exposed Module Federation module should normally have this shape:"},"64":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-18","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#protocol-identity","content":"The default expose is `./application`; callers can choose another expose in `AppRef`."},"65":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-19","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"Invariants:"},"66":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-20","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"`identity.instanceId` is unique while its mount transaction or retained instance record exists."},"67":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-21","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"the `props` reference is captured when the mount transaction starts, but Fronts does not clone or\nfreeze the caller's object. Callers and producers must treat it as read-only shared input."},"68":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-22","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"`services` contains only declared and authorized capabilities."},"69":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-23","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"`signal` aborts when mounting is cancelled or the instance is force-aborted."},"70":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-24","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"`target` is supplied and controlled by the selected container for the lifetime of this mount."},"71":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-25","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#mount-input","content":"a producer must render only inside its target unless a declared platform capability explicitly\npermits another effect."},"72":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-26","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#ready","content":"`mount()` means resources were accepted; `ready` means the application committed its usable UI.\nIf omitted, the application is ready as soon as `mount()` returns. Hosts impose a deadline."},"73":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-27","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#ready","content":"Readiness must reject on initial render failure. It must not wait for optional analytics,\nbackground data, or an interaction that may never happen. Replacement commits only after\nreadiness succeeds."},"74":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-28","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#updateprops","content":"Updates an existing mounted application without changing identity, deployment, target, or service\nscope. Implementations should resolve after the framework commits the update. When unsupported,\nthe host reports a typed lifecycle failure instead of silently remounting."},"75":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-29","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#activate-and-deactivate","content":"Optional visibility/activity hints. They are not mount/unmount and must preserve application\nstate. Typical uses are pausing timers, subscriptions, media, or expensive rendering while a tab\nis inactive."},"76":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-30","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#unmount","content":"Required and treated as idempotent by the host boundary. It must remove render roots, listeners,\ntimers, observers, subscriptions, and producer-owned DOM. It must not remove the container element;\nthe container adapter owns that resource."},"77":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-31","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#state-machine","content":"Operations are serialized per instance. Calls that are invalid for the current state reject with\na `FrontsError`; they are never silently queued across destruction. Clean failed/aborted\ntransactions release their host record after rollback; incomplete cleanup remains visible to\n`host.audit()` without inventing a later `destroyed` transition."},"78":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-32","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#cancellation","content":"An external mount signal is combined with an instance-owned signal. Aborting either prevents later\nphases from starting and triggers rollback. Loaders and resolvers receive the signal and should\npass it to network requests. Application code must listen when it starts long-running work."},"79":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-33","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#cancellation","content":"Aborting is cooperative: JavaScript already evaluated in the same realm cannot be forcibly\nstopped. Stronger runtime isolation requires an iframe and ultimately destroying that child realm."},"80":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-34","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"Applications declare string keys:"},"81":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-35","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"Declaration is necessary but not sufficient. The host's `capabilityPolicy` evaluates each key for\nthe concrete application identity and receives the instance `signal`. The runtime stops awaiting\nasynchronous authorization when that signal aborts. A declared capability that is unavailable or\ndenied rejects an ordinary application mount; undeclared services never enter its facade. A service\nscope is revoked on cleanup, so retained method proxies fail rather than continuing to affect the\nhost."},"82":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-36","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"Static `services` remain the simplest host configuration. When a capability must be bound to one\napplication instance, use `createServices` as an instance-level provider:"},"83":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-37","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"The provider runs once per mount/replace transaction after resolution and application validation.\nIts frozen `capabilities` list contains declarations, not grants. Provider services override static\nservices with the same key; the host then applies availability checks and `capabilityPolicy`, and\nonly the requested, authorized keys enter the application facade."},"84":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-38","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"Returning the result transfers ownership to the host. `dispose` is called at most once after\nfacade revocation, including authorization failure, aborted mount, ordinary unmount, and host\nshutdown. It may be asynchronous; a failure is surfaced as an unmount cleanup failure without\nskipping container disposal. An aborted mount stops awaiting a pending provider; if its result\narrives later, the host disposes it and keeps that cleanup visible as a pending operation. Providers\nmust still honor `signal` to stop work promptly. If a provider throws before returning its result,\nit still owns rollback of any partially allocated resources."},"85":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-39","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"For iframe applications, `IframeProxyLoaderOptions.capabilities` is a host-controlled maximum,\nnot a list of mandatory dependencies and not the final child grant. Entries unavailable from the\ninstance service provider or denied by policy are omitted from the parent offer rather than failing\nthe proxy before the child is known. After loading the real child application, the agent negotiates\nits declared subset with the parent. Only the exact negotiated intersection becomes RPC stubs, and\nthe parent checks that grant on every call. A child is still rejected when one of its own declared\nrequirements is absent from that offer."},"86":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-40","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#capabilities","content":"Prefer narrow intent APIs such as `navigation.go()` and `telemetry.emit()` over ambient objects\nsuch as `window`, a Redux store, or a generic message bus."},"87":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-41","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#react","content":"`defineReactApp()` owns a React root, context, error boundary, commit-based readiness, prop updates,\noptional Strict Mode, and root unmount. Host services and identity are available through hooks."},"88":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-42","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#vue-3","content":"`defineVueApp()` owns a Vue app, provided context, reactive prop updates, `nextTick()` readiness,\nconfiguration hook, and app unmount. It creates an inner element when mounting into Shadow DOM."},"89":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-43","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#vue-3","content":"These adapters intentionally expose fewer framework-specific features than the official MF\nBridge. Use official Bridge directly when its routing/data/SSR integration is the actual\nrequirement; use Fronts adapters when the application must participate in the Fronts host ABI."},"90":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-44","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#compatibility-rule","content":"Protocol major versions are strict. A host must reject an unknown major rather than trying to\nguess behavior. New optional handle methods can be added compatibly; changing mount semantics,\nreadiness, service authorization, or cleanup ownership requires a new protocol major."},"91":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-45","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#verification","content":"`pnpm exec vitest run packages/core/test/app.test.ts packages/core/test/host.test.ts` verifies\nprotocol branding, application validation, lifecycle ordering, readiness, and cleanup."},"92":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-46","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#verification","content":"`pnpm exec vitest run packages/core/test/services.test.ts packages/core/test/iframe.test.ts`\nverifies capability scoping, provider cleanup, and the negotiated iframe service contract."},"93":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-47","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#verification","content":"`packages/core/src/app` is the public protocol source of truth."},"94":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract-48","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/application-contract#verification","content":"`packages/react/test` and `packages/vue3/test`\nverify that framework producers implement the same contract."},"95":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"page","content":"Fronts 2.0 Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Core concepts","Core concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture"},"96":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-0","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","content":"Runtime layers, ownership boundaries, dependency direction, mount transactions, replacement, and extension points."},"97":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-1","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#system-boundary","content":"System boundary"},"98":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-2","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#dependency-rule","content":"Dependency rule"},"99":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-3","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#core-abstractions","content":"Core abstractions"},"100":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-4","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#appref","content":"`AppRef`"},"101":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-5","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#resolvecontext","content":"`ResolveContext`"},"102":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-6","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#resolvedappsource","content":"`ResolvedApp<Source>`"},"103":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-7","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#apploadersource","content":"`AppLoader<Source>`"},"104":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-8","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#containeradapter","content":"`ContainerAdapter`"},"105":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-9","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#frontsapp","content":"`FrontsApp`"},"106":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-10","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#frontshost","content":"`FrontsHost`"},"107":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-11","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Ownership compared with Module Federation 2"},"108":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-12","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Host mount transaction"},"109":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-13","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"Replacement transaction"},"110":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-14","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Extension points"},"111":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-15","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#verification","content":"Verification"},"112":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-16","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#system-boundary","content":"Fronts turns an application reference into a governed application instance. It is deliberately\nsplit into layers so that release policy, transport, rendering framework, and execution isolation\ncan evolve independently."},"113":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-17","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#dependency-rule","content":"Dependencies point inward:"},"114":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-18","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#dependency-rule","content":"`@fronts/core` has no framework, bundler, or Module Federation dependency."},"115":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-19","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#dependency-rule","content":"`@fronts/mf` depends on core and peers on the public `@module-federation/runtime` package."},"116":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-20","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#dependency-rule","content":"`@fronts/react` and `@fronts/vue3` depend on core and peer on their rendering framework."},"117":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-21","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#dependency-rule","content":"Examples compose packages; packages never import examples or platform policy."},"118":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-22","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#dependency-rule","content":"No Fronts source may import `@module-federation/runtime-core`. The public Runtime package is the\ncompatibility boundary. The official `@module-federation/enhanced/runtime` entry re-exports the\nsame runtime through `runtime-tools`; a pure runtime consumer can depend directly on\n`@module-federation/runtime`, which avoids pulling in build-plugin concerns. See the audited\nruntime source\nand runtime-tools re-export."},"119":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-23","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#appref","content":"A logical request: name, expose, optional semantic range, and optional release channel. It does not\ncontain a CDN URL."},"120":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-24","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#resolvecontext","content":"Request policy inputs: environment, tenant, cohort, and metadata, plus an immutable host operation\nenvelope. The host does not interpret policy fields; a resolver or registry owns selection policy.\nThe operation envelope carries correlation and cancellation across extension boundaries."},"121":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-25","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#resolvedappsource","content":"An immutable decision containing the normalized reference, transport-specific source, selected\nversion, and optional metadata. This object is the handoff between policy and loading.\nThe host snapshots and freezes the decision envelope, reference, and top-level metadata. The\ntransport source remains opaque; adapters must treat it as read-only and own any internal state."},"122":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-26","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#apploadersource","content":"A transport adapter with `load()` and optional `preload()`. A loader returns an unknown module;\nthe host validates the Fronts application protocol before mounting it. Its context identifies the\nhost action and includes an application identity only for mount/replace transactions."},"123":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-27","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#containeradapter","content":"Prepares an execution target and owns its cleanup. A container can also select a different loader;\niframe execution uses this to ensure code is loaded inside the child realm instead of the parent.\nThe mount request may provide a static container or a resolution-aware container resolver.\nPlanning happens before loader selection; preparation receives the resolved deployment and the\ncorrelated application operation context used for resolution and loading."},"124":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-28","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#frontsapp","content":"The framework-neutral producer contract. React and Vue are adapters that create this contract,\nnot special host modes."},"125":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-29","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#frontshost","content":"The stateful orchestrator. It resolves, loads, validates, creates a service scope, prepares a\ncontainer, mounts, waits for readiness, exposes lifecycle controls, replaces instances, emits\nevents, and audits retained resources."},"126":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-30","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Capability"},"127":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-31","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"MF 2"},"128":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-32","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Fronts"},"129":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-33","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Manifest/Snapshot and asset graph"},"130":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-34","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"131":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-35","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Consumes as opaque runtime behavior"},"132":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-36","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Remote registration and expose loading"},"133":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-37","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"134":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-38","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Calls public instance methods through adapter"},"135":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-39","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Shared dependency selection"},"136":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-40","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"137":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-41","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not intercept"},"138":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-42","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Runtime loading hooks and plugins"},"139":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-43","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"140":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-44","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"May correlate at its boundary"},"141":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-45","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Remote type generation/download"},"142":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-46","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"143":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-47","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not replace"},"144":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-48","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Framework bridge render/destroy"},"145":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-49","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Official Bridge owns for Bridge apps"},"146":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-50","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Own ABI adapters only"},"147":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-51","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Logical app-to-deployment policy"},"148":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-52","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not prescribe"},"149":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-53","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns resolver contract"},"150":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-54","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Cross-transport lifecycle state"},"151":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-55","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not prescribe"},"152":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-56","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"153":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-57","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"DOM/Shadow/iframe container policy"},"154":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-58","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not prescribe"},"155":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-59","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"156":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-60","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Host service authorization"},"157":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-61","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not prescribe"},"158":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-62","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"159":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-63","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Ready-gated application replacement"},"160":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-64","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not prescribe"},"161":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-65","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"162":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-66","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Application instance leak audit"},"163":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-67","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Does not prescribe"},"164":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-68","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"Owns"},"165":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-69","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#ownership-compared-with-module-federation-2","content":"MF runtime plugins remain the right extension point for URL rewriting, manifest fetch behavior,\nscript/link creation, shared resolution, and remote-load fallback. Fronts resolvers remain the\nright extension point for business deployment policy. Mixing those concerns makes both layers\nharder to reason about. See the official runtime plugin guide."},"166":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-70","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"The host executes these phases in order:"},"167":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-71","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Normalize the reference and create operation, identity, and trace IDs."},"168":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-72","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Resolve the deployment."},"169":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-73","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Resolve a dynamic container request when configured, choose the default or container-specific\nloader from that request, and load the module."},"170":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-74","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Validate protocol name/version and application shape."},"171":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-75","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Create instance-bound services when configured, authorize declared capabilities, and create a\nrevocable service scope."},"172":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-76","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Prepare the container."},"173":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-77","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Call `mount()` with the captured read-only props reference, scoped services, target, identity,\nand abort signal."},"174":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-78","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Wait for the application `ready` promise with a deadline."},"175":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-79","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Publish the instance as usable."},"176":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-80","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#host-mount-transaction","content":"Failure unwinds every acquired resource in deterministic lifecycle order. The original error\nremains primary; cleanup errors are reported through typed Fronts errors and events."},"177":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-81","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"`replace(currentInstanceId, nextOptions)` is intentionally not an in-place remote mutation:"},"178":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-82","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"A hidden staging slot is created inside `nextOptions.target`; pass the current layout parent for\nan in-place visual replacement, or another target for an intentional move."},"179":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-83","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"The next deployment resolves, loads, mounts, and reaches `ready` in staging."},"180":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-84","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"If any phase fails, staging is destroyed and the current instance stays active."},"181":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-85","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"If ready succeeds, the new slot is committed, then the previous instance is unmounted."},"182":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-86","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"A previous cleanup failure is returned separately; it does not pretend the new application\nfailed to become ready."},"183":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-87","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#replacement-transaction","content":"Concurrent replacement of one instance is rejected. This gives the platform a clear transaction\nboundary without mutating MF runtime caches behind an active application."},"184":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-88","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Implement `AppResolver` for a deployment registry or experiment service."},"185":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-89","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Implement `ResolutionCache` for shared or persistent policy caching."},"186":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-90","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Use a container request resolver when registry metadata selects DOM, Shadow DOM, or a dedicated\niframe origin per deployment."},"187":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-91","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Implement `AppLoader` for a non-MF transport."},"188":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-92","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Implement `ContainerAdapter` for another execution target."},"189":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-93","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Subscribe to `HostEvent` and map it to OpenTelemetry or an internal telemetry pipeline."},"190":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-94","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Use `createServices` for instance-bound capability implementations and deterministic cleanup."},"191":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-95","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Use `capabilityPolicy` for tenant, identity, or deployment-specific authorization."},"192":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-96","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#extension-points","content":"Extension points are explicit objects, not process-wide globals."},"193":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-97","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#verification","content":"`pnpm check` verifies package boundaries, public exports, types, lifecycle contracts, and test\ncoverage across the workspace."},"194":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-98","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#verification","content":"`pnpm test:e2e` and `pnpm test:e2e:preview` verify the documented composition against development\nservers and fresh production output."},"195":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-99","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#verification","content":"`packages/core/src` owns the framework- and transport-neutral runtime."},"196":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture-100","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/architecture#verification","content":"`packages/mf/src` demonstrates the transport adapter boundary over the\nofficial Module Federation Runtime API."},"197":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","type":"page","content":"Fronts 2.0 after Module Federation 2","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Core concepts","Core concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record"},"198":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-0","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","content":"Decision, alternatives, ownership boundaries, non-goals, and release criteria for retaining a Fronts application runtime."},"199":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-1","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision","content":"Decision"},"200":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-2","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#official-bridge-overlap","content":"Official Bridge overlap"},"201":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-3","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Decision matrix"},"202":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-4","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#accepted-ownership-boundary","content":"Accepted ownership boundary"},"203":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-5","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#release-criteria","content":"Release criteria"},"204":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-6","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#verification","content":"Verification"},"205":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-7","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","content":"Status: accepted for the 2.0 alpha. Reviewed on 2026-07-13 against Module Federation 2.7 and the\nprovided `module-federation/core` source at commit\n`37c97f6ec`."},"206":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-8","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision","content":"Fronts 2.0 has independent value only when it does not duplicate mature Module Federation\ncapabilities. MF already provides an independent Runtime, manifests and snapshots, preloading,\nruntime plugins, dynamic types, DevTools, shared-dependency selection, and React/Vue Bridges.\nWrapping `remoteEntry`, creating another share resolver, or renaming a React remote application\nwould make Fronts a fragile fork."},"207":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-9","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision","content":"The remaining gap is one layer higher. An enterprise host must turn a remote module into a governed\napplication instance: stable lifecycle, tenant and release policy, multiple isolation containers,\nleast-privilege host capabilities, ready-gated replacement, rollback, cancellation, and\ncross-framework observability. MF owns reliable module delivery; application policy should not be\nforced into that layer."},"208":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-10","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision","content":"Fronts 2.0 is therefore a transport-neutral, framework-neutral application runtime and\norchestration layer above Module Federation. It is neither another MF Runtime nor a complete\nmicro-frontend cloud platform."},"209":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-11","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#official-bridge-overlap","content":"The official React Bridge already exports, loads, renders, and destroys complete React applications\nwith routing and data-prefetch support; Vue 3 Bridge follows the same direction. A React/Vue-only\nsystem that needs no platform governance should use the official Bridge directly."},"210":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-12","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#official-bridge-overlap","content":"`@fronts/react` and `@fronts/vue3` are producers for the Fronts ABI, not replacements for those\nBridges. Fronts is justified by the combined value of its framework-neutral Host, resolver,\ncontainers, capability scopes, replacement transaction, and governance. Optional Bridge-to-Fronts\nadapters may be added later without coupling core to Bridge internals."},"211":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-13","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Situation"},"212":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-14","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Recommendation"},"213":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-15","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Load a shared utility or component"},"214":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-16","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Use MF Runtime directly"},"215":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-17","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Official Bridge already satisfies a React/Vue application"},"216":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-18","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Use MF Bridge"},"217":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-19","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"One framework, one trust domain, fixed remote addresses"},"218":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-20","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Fronts is usually unnecessary"},"219":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-21","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Govern mount, update, and cleanup across frameworks"},"220":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-22","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Fronts"},"221":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-23","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Select versions by environment, tenant, cohort, or channel"},"222":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-24","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Fronts resolver plus an external registry"},"223":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-25","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Use one Host API for DOM, Shadow DOM, and iframe"},"224":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-26","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Fronts containers"},"225":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-27","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Restrict host APIs by declaration and policy"},"226":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-28","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Fronts service scopes"},"227":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-29","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Replace only after a candidate is ready and retain the current app on failure"},"228":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-30","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#decision-matrix","content":"Fronts replacement transaction"},"229":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-31","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#accepted-ownership-boundary","content":"Fronts owns the application ABI (`mount → ready → update/activate/deactivate → unmount`), per-instance\nstate and cancellation, immutable deployment resolution, container selection, scoped services,\nready-gated replacement, lifecycle events, leak audit, and framework adapters."},"230":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-32","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#accepted-ownership-boundary","content":"Module Federation continues to own remote registration, manifests and snapshots, expose and asset\nloading, preloading, shared dependency selection, runtime plugins and low-level hooks, generated\ntypes, DevTools, and bundler integration."},"231":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-33","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#accepted-ownership-boundary","content":"The MVP explicitly excludes a bundler plugin, another shared resolver, mutation of MF global\nsnapshots, third-party CSS rewriting, a complete JavaScript sandbox, registry SaaS, a router\nreplacement, SSR/RSC orchestration, and an implicit global event bus."},"232":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-34","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#release-criteria","content":"Fronts 2.0 is worth publishing only if `@fronts/mf` uses public official Runtime APIs; core stays\nindependent from frameworks and bundlers; every container and failure phase has contract tests; a\nreal Runtime loads a real remote; replacement failure preserves the usable instance; iframe\nmessaging never uses wildcard `targetOrigin`; capabilities constrain services; public package\nsubpaths work through ESM and CommonJS; and a clean install/build/test/release check is repeatable."},"233":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-35","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#release-criteria","content":"If the official Runtime or Bridges later absorb these responsibilities completely, Fronts should\nshrink or retire instead of preserving overlap for its own sake."},"234":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record-36","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/decision-record#verification","content":"The MF integration matrix,\nHost Runtime API,\napplication contract, and\nisolation model map each retained responsibility to a public\ncontract. `pnpm check`, development E2E, and production-preview E2E verify executable criteria;\npublication and human security gates remain documented under operations."},"235":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","type":"page","content":"Fumadocs static website on GitHub Pages","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Core concepts","Core concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision"},"236":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-0","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","content":"Decision to build explicit bilingual static routes on main and replace gh-pages with one generated root commit."},"237":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-1","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#context","content":"Context"},"238":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-2","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#decision","content":"Decision"},"239":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-3","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"240":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-4","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"241":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-5","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#security-and-operations","content":"Security and operations"},"242":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-6","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#verification","content":"Verification"},"243":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-7","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#context","content":"Fronts needs current English and Chinese documentation without coupling package publication to a\ndocumentation server. The custom domain already points at GitHub Pages, but the existing branch\ncontains a six-year-old Docusaurus artifact. The repository's package release workflow still uses\n`master`, while the requested website source branch is `main`."},"244":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-8","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#context","content":"The site needs nested technical navigation, MDX, diagrams, source links, localized search, static\nhosting, deterministic deployment, and a way to prove which source commit is online."},"245":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-9","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#decision","content":"Use Fumadocs with Next.js `output: 'export'`. Source lives in the `website` pnpm workspace on\n`main`; package publication remains on `master`. Routes use explicit `/en` and `/zh` prefixes with\ndirectory-based content parsing and no locale fallback. Search is a generated static Orama endpoint,\nwith the Mandarin tokenizer for Chinese."},"246":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-10","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#decision","content":"Publish `website/out` to `gh-pages` as a new parentless commit on every deployment. Preserve the\ncurrent `CNAME` blob exactly, add `.nojekyll`, and push with `force-with-lease` tied to the fetched\nremote SHA. Embed the full `main` Git revision in every application page and poll the custom domain\nuntil that revision appears."},"247":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-11","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#alternatives-considered","content":"Keep the previous Docusaurus output: rejected because its content and build provenance no longer\nrepresent Fronts 2.0."},"248":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-12","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#alternatives-considered","content":"Keep authored English and Chinese copies for every page: rejected for canonical English contracts\nbecause duplication would drift; source mapping plus explicit Chinese pages makes ownership clear."},"249":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-13","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#alternatives-considered","content":"Infer locale with middleware, cookies, or redirects: rejected because static GitHub Pages cannot\nprovide a reliable server negotiation layer and explicit URLs are easier to cache and share."},"250":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-14","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#alternatives-considered","content":"Publish through a persistent `gh-pages` history: rejected because generated history has no review\nvalue; the reviewed source history is on `main`, while one root commit proves the exact live tree."},"251":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-15","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#alternatives-considered","content":"Use only a Pages artifact deployment: rejected for this repository because the requested contract\nexplicitly retains a `gh-pages` CNAME and branch-visible static output."},"252":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-16","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#alternatives-considered","content":"Add the website to the package release branch/workflow: rejected because documentation deployment\nand npm publication have different permissions, rollback, and release cadence."},"253":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-17","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#consequences","content":"The website is serverless after export, keeps the current custom domain, and can be reproduced from\none reviewed source commit. English canonical changes automatically reach the generated tree, while\nChinese translations remain an explicit review responsibility. A separate workflow can verify and\ndeploy docs without widening npm release permissions."},"254":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-18","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#consequences","content":"The generated branch is intentionally rewritten, so it is not a durable rollback history. Recovery\nmeans rebuilding a known-good `main` revision and publishing another root commit. Search and Mermaid\nmust remain compatible with static export. Adding a language requires content inventory, tokenizer,\nnavigation, metadata, output checks, and browser evidence rather than only a locale label."},"255":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-19","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#security-and-operations","content":"The deploy script refuses dirty, unpushed, or non-`main` sources. Its exact lease prevents silently\noverwriting a concurrent Pages update. It reads CNAME from the currently fetched remote commit and\ncompares the new blob byte-for-byte before push. The GitHub workflow receives only `contents: write`;\nit does not receive npm OIDC or release secrets."},"256":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-20","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#security-and-operations","content":"Online revision polling distinguishes a successful Git push from a successful Pages publication.\nThe first rollout still requires human review of Pages branch/root settings, domain/TLS state, the\nroot commit, language navigation, and public article rendering."},"257":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-21","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#verification","content":"`pnpm website:check` verifies content, MDX/TypeScript, static export, links, assets, search, and\nbrowser behavior."},"258":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-22","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#verification","content":"`scripts/deploy-website.mjs` verifies branch/source state,\nCNAME preservation, parentless commit construction, exact lease, remote SHA, and online revision."},"259":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-23","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#verification","content":"`.github/workflows/docs.yml` executes the checked deployment\nfrom `main` with Node 24 and Chromium."},"260":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-24","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#verification","content":"`website/README.md` documents local ownership and operator commands."},"261":{"id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision-25","page_id":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/concepts/documentation-website-decision#verification","content":"Verification of repository Pages settings and custom-domain TLS remains an external human check."},"262":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing to Fronts","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Operate and release","Operate and release"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing"},"263":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-0","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","content":"Development setup, change boundaries, testing, documentation, Changesets, and review expectations for Fronts contributors."},"264":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-1","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#development-prerequisites","content":"Development prerequisites"},"265":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-2","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Repository map"},"266":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-3","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Change workflow"},"267":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-4","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Changesets"},"268":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-5","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#focused-development-commands","content":"Focused development commands"},"269":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-6","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"Browser E2E"},"270":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-7","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"Adding or changing public APIs"},"271":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-8","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"Module Federation changes"},"272":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-9","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"Iframe and capability changes"},"273":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-10","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"Documentation changes"},"274":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-11","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"Pull request checklist"},"275":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-12","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#reporting-problems","content":"Reporting problems"},"276":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-13","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#verification","content":"Verification"},"277":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-14","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#development-prerequisites","content":"Node.js 22.18 or newer;"},"278":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-15","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#development-prerequisites","content":"pnpm 10 or 11 through Corepack;"},"279":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-16","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#development-prerequisites","content":"a Chromium installation managed by Playwright for browser E2E;"},"280":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-17","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#development-prerequisites","content":"macOS, Linux, or another environment capable of running the repository's Node and browser tools."},"281":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-18","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#development-prerequisites","content":"The root `package.json` is the source of truth for engines and the pinned package\nmanager. CI runs the main check on Node 22 and 24."},"282":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-19","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#development-prerequisites","content":"Do not replace pnpm with npm or Yarn when changing the workspace lockfile."},"283":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-20","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Area"},"284":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-21","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Responsibility"},"285":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-22","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`packages/core`"},"286":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-23","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Application protocol, Host, resolvers, containers, services, errors, and iframe transport."},"287":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-24","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`packages/mf`"},"288":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-25","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Adapter over the public official Module Federation runtime instance API."},"289":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-26","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`packages/react`"},"290":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-27","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"React producer and Host adapter for the Fronts application contract."},"291":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-28","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`packages/vue3`"},"292":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-29","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Vue 3 producer and Host adapter for the same contract."},"293":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-30","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`examples`"},"294":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-31","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Executable core-only, framework, iframe, Rsbuild, and Vite integration evidence."},"295":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-32","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`e2e`"},"296":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-33","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Playwright behavior shared by development and production-preview server modes."},"297":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-34","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`docs`"},"298":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-35","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Architecture, contracts, operations, support boundaries, and runbooks."},"299":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-36","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"`.changeset`"},"300":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-37","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Pending public-package release notes and prerelease state."},"301":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-38","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#repository-map","content":"Read Architecture and the\nApplication contract before changing package boundaries or\nlifecycle semantics."},"302":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-39","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Start from an up-to-date branch and confirm the worktree contains no changes you do not own."},"303":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-40","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Reproduce the behavior or define the contract before editing implementation."},"304":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-41","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Change one concern at a time and add the narrowest test that proves it."},"305":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-42","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Update every affected public README, contract, architecture document, runbook, and example."},"306":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-43","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Add a Changeset when a published package changes for consumers."},"307":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-44","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Run focused checks while iterating, then the complete required gates."},"308":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-45","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Review the diff for unrelated formatting, generated artifacts, secrets, and accidental public API\nexpansion."},"309":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-46","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Keep commits focused. One independently reviewable concern per commit is preferred. Existing history\nuses Conventional Commit-style subjects such as:"},"310":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-47","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#change-workflow","content":"Do not rewrite or discard another contributor's worktree changes. Do not commit build output,\nPlaywright reports, coverage output, package tarballs, or local environment files unless a task\nexplicitly changes their source-controlled policy."},"311":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-48","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Every consumer-visible change to one or more public packages needs a Changeset:"},"312":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-49","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Select all affected packages and describe user impact rather than implementation detail. The four\npublic packages are a fixed Changesets group, so versioning remains synchronized while the 2.0\ncontract stabilizes."},"313":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-50","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Typical Changeset decisions:"},"314":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-51","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Change"},"315":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-52","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Changeset?"},"316":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-53","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Public runtime behavior, error, export, type, peer range, package metadata, or security fix"},"317":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-54","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Yes"},"318":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-55","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Internal refactor with identical published behavior"},"319":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-56","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Usually no; add one if consumers can observe it"},"320":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-57","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Test-only or example-only verification"},"321":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-58","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"No, unless it accompanies a package behavior change"},"322":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-59","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Documentation-only correction outside packed package READMEs"},"323":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-60","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"No"},"324":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-61","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Public package README change that affects consumer guidance"},"325":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-62","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Yes when released package content changes materially"},"326":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-63","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#changesets","content":"Do not edit package versions or changelogs by hand. The Changesets release flow owns them."},"327":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-64","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#focused-development-commands","content":"Run a focused Vitest file while iterating:"},"328":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-65","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#focused-development-commands","content":"Run the complete non-browser gate before handoff:"},"329":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-66","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#focused-development-commands","content":"`pnpm check` runs formatting/lint, a clean topological build, isolated packed-package consumption,\nTypeScript checks, unit/integration tests, and coverage thresholds. Do not treat a focused test as\nevidence that the repository gate passes."},"330":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-67","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"Install the configured Chromium binary once:"},"331":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-68","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"Development-server mode:"},"332":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-69","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"Fresh production build and preview mode:"},"333":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-70","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"CI requires the production-preview path. Run both when changing Host orchestration, remote output,\nasset URLs, manifests, shared dependencies, iframe behavior, framework adapters, or example server\nconfiguration."},"334":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-71","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"The current server map is owned by `e2e/playwright-config.ts`:"},"335":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-72","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"`4100`–`4103`: React Host, React remote, Vue remote, and iframe agent;"},"336":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-73","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"`4110`: core-only Host;"},"337":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-74","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"`4200`–`4203`: plain Vite Host and the official, unscoped, and OriginJS producers."},"338":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-75","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#browser-e2e","content":"The OriginJS workspace's `dev` command intentionally builds and previews its remote. It does not\nprovide a bundleless remote dev mode."},"339":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-76","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"A public API change is incomplete until all applicable evidence exists:"},"340":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-77","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"implementation and types are exported only through an intended package `exports` entry;"},"341":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-78","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"unit/contract tests cover success, failure, cancellation, and cleanup;"},"342":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-79","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"package README and the relevant contract guide explain intent and boundaries;"},"343":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-80","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"runtime identifiers, input envelopes, and extension contexts follow existing validation and\nsnapshot rules;"},"344":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-81","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"ESM and CommonJS packed-package imports still pass;"},"345":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-82","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"a Changeset records consumer impact;"},"346":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-83","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"compatibility and rollback implications are reviewed before stable."},"347":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-84","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#adding-or-changing-public-apis","content":"Avoid adding a convenience API that bypasses the Host transaction. Standalone development should\ncompose a normal Host with a static resolver and local loader so readiness, services, cancellation,\nand cleanup remain identical to production."},"348":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-85","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"`@fronts/mf` MUST remain an adapter over public official runtime instance methods. It must not:"},"349":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-86","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"parse or mutate MF manifests/snapshots;"},"350":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-87","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"import private `runtime-core` internals;"},"351":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-88","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"implement shared dependency selection;"},"352":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-89","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"discover or mutate a hidden global default instance;"},"353":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-90","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"add bundler-specific behavior to `@fronts/core`."},"354":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-91","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#module-federation-changes","content":"When adding a producer compatibility claim, follow the acceptance checklist in\nModule Federation integrations. A load-only smoke test is\ninsufficient: prove readiness, services, update, unmount, idle audit, production output, and shared\nbehavior where applicable."},"355":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-92","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"Iframe, identity, capability, and service-scope changes are security-sensitive. Preserve these\ninvariants:"},"356":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-93","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"exact origins; never `targetOrigin=\"*\"`;"},"357":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-94","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"dedicated child origin with the required sandbox tokens;"},"358":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-95","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"validation of both message origin and expected source window;"},"359":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-96","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"random channel ID and exactly one transferred port;"},"360":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-97","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"final grant as the intersection of proxy maximum, Host-authorized services, and child declaration;"},"361":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-98","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"parent-side validation on every privileged call;"},"362":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-99","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"revocation on abort/unmount and deterministic provider, peer, agent, and container cleanup."},"363":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-100","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#iframe-and-capability-changes","content":"Run the complete iframe tests and cross-origin browser E2E. Review\nIframe deployment,\nIsolation and security, and SECURITY.md. Security\nreports must not be moved into a public issue or normal pull request before coordinated disclosure."},"364":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-101","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"Documentation should capture intent, ownership boundaries, invariants, trade-offs, and verification\npaths rather than restating implementation line by line."},"365":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-102","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"For a new concept document under `docs`:"},"366":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-103","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"add YAML frontmatter with `type`, `title`, `description`, `owner`, and `status`;"},"367":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-104","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"use `status: proposed` until maintainers accept new policy or design commitments;"},"368":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-105","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"link source types/tests instead of copying volatile field lists and defaults;"},"369":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-106","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"include a `## Verification` section with commands or explicit missing evidence;"},"370":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-107","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"add it to `docs/index.md` and link that index from any relevant package README;"},"371":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-108","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"use Mermaid only when it materially clarifies a boundary, sequence, lifecycle, or decision tree;"},"372":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-109","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"run `pnpm docs:check` and Prettier so relative links, metadata, API coverage, and navigation remain\nvalid."},"373":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-110","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#documentation-changes","content":"Update documentation in the same concern commit as the behavior that makes it stale. Do not add\npre-2.0 migration or compatibility material to current Fronts 2.0 documentation."},"374":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-111","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"The change has one clear responsibility and no unrelated worktree edits."},"375":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-112","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"Public behavior has focused success, failure, cancellation, and cleanup evidence."},"376":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-113","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"`pnpm check` passes."},"377":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-114","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"`pnpm docs:check` passes when Markdown or public Host types changed."},"378":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-115","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"Relevant development and production-preview E2E pass."},"379":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-116","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"Public package changes include a Changeset."},"380":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-117","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"READMEs, contracts, support tables, and runbooks match the new behavior."},"381":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-118","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"New producer claims state their exact tested boundary."},"382":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-119","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"Security-sensitive changes received explicit human review."},"383":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-120","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"Logs, fixtures, screenshots, and reports contain no credentials or tenant-sensitive data."},"384":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-121","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#pull-request-checklist","content":"The commit history is focused and reviewable."},"385":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-122","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#reporting-problems","content":"Use GitHub issues for reproducible bugs, documentation gaps, and feature proposals. Include the\ndiagnostic evidence requested by Troubleshooting and\nSupport policy."},"386":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-123","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#reporting-problems","content":"Do not report vulnerabilities publicly. Follow SECURITY.md."},"387":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-124","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#verification","content":"`package.json` owns required commands, engines, and package-manager configuration."},"388":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-125","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#verification","content":"CI owns the Node and Chromium release gates."},"389":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-126","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#verification","content":"Releasing owns Changesets, prerelease, provenance, and publication flow."},"390":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-127","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#verification","content":"`pnpm check` is the complete local non-browser gate."},"391":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing-128","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/contributing#verification","content":"`pnpm test:e2e` and `pnpm test:e2e:preview` prove development and built example composition."},"392":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"page","content":"Bilingual documentation website","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Operate and release","Operate and release"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website"},"393":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-0","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","content":"Content, static-export, search, verification, and deployment contract for fronts.js.org."},"394":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-1","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#problem-and-outcome","content":"Problem and outcome"},"395":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-2","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#content-contract","content":"Content contract"},"396":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-3","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"Reader contract"},"397":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-4","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"Acceptance criteria"},"398":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-5","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#rollout-and-rollback","content":"Rollout and rollback"},"399":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-6","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#risks-and-reviewer-focus","content":"Risks and reviewer focus"},"400":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-7","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#verification","content":"Verification"},"401":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-8","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#problem-and-outcome","content":"The repository's canonical Markdown is complete enough for maintainers but does not provide a\nsearchable, navigable, bilingual reader experience. The previous `gh-pages` site is an obsolete\nDocusaurus build and is not generated from the current Fronts 2.0 contracts."},"402":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-9","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#problem-and-outcome","content":"The outcome is a Fumadocs website sourced on `main`, statically exported, and published at\n`https://fronts.js.org/`. It presents the current application ABI, Host Runtime, Module Federation\nboundary, isolation model, package guides, operations, compatibility policy, troubleshooting,\ncontribution, release, and security guidance in English and Chinese."},"403":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-10","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#content-contract","content":"`website/content/content-map.json` is the inventory.\nEvery slug has exactly one English and one Chinese page. Canonical English technical content is\nsynchronized from repository documents and public package READMEs; authored English overrides are\nallowed only when a canonical source is not a complete English website article. Chinese pages are\nmaintained explicitly rather than machine-falling back to English."},"404":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-11","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#content-contract","content":"Generated `website/content/docs` is disposable and ignored. Source documents remain authoritative\nfor precise APIs, package exports, engine ranges, and peer dependencies. Website generation may\nrewrite repository-relative links to localized routes or immutable GitHub `main` links, but it must\nnot invent a second API contract."},"405":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-12","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"`/` offers explicit English and Chinese entry points."},"406":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-13","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"`/en/` and `/zh/` are localized product overviews."},"407":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-14","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"`/en/docs/` and `/zh/docs/` expose parallel navigation trees with trailing-slash-compatible URLs."},"408":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-15","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"Each article publishes canonical and alternate-language metadata."},"409":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-16","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"English search uses the static Orama index; Chinese search uses the Mandarin tokenizer."},"410":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-17","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"Mermaid diagrams render client-side without requiring a documentation server."},"411":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-18","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"Each application HTML page embeds the complete source Git revision as `fronts-revision` metadata."},"412":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-19","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"The layout links back to the corresponding source file on the repository's `main` branch."},"413":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-20","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#reader-contract","content":"The site does not silently redirect by cookie or browser language. Explicit locale routes keep the\nexport deterministic on GitHub Pages and make shared links stable."},"414":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-21","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"Content generation produces 22 English/Chinese page pairs and rejects any unmapped canonical\ndocument anywhere below `docs`."},"415":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-22","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"Every localized page has title, description, source path, substantial content, and multiple\nsections; the Chinese tree contains Chinese content and no `/en/docs` links."},"416":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-23","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"A clean `next build` exports the root, both homes, all 40 documentation routes, and static search."},"417":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-24","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"Static output validation proves all expected routes and local assets exist, each application\npage has the correct HTML language and source revision, and both search indexes contain the Host\nRuntime guide."},"418":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-25","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"Chromium E2E proves the language selector, both documentation roots, a deep runtime article, and\nEnglish and Mandarin search."},"419":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-26","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"Deployment is allowed only from a clean `main` commit equal to `origin/main`."},"420":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-27","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"Deployment preserves the existing `gh-pages:CNAME` byte-for-byte and publishes the export plus\n`.nojekyll` in a commit with no parent."},"421":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-28","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#acceptance-criteria","content":"The branch update uses an exact force lease, verifies the resulting remote SHA, and succeeds only\nafter the custom domain serves the embedded source revision."},"422":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-29","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#rollout-and-rollback","content":"The initial rollout replaces the previous `gh-pages` history only after local verification and a\nsuccessful push of `main`. The deploy script records both the prior branch SHA and the new root\ndeployment SHA in command output. GitHub Pages continues using the existing custom domain because\nthe original CNAME blob is preserved exactly."},"423":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-30","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#rollout-and-rollback","content":"For a documentation regression, fix or revert the source commit on `main` and redeploy, producing a\nnew verified root commit. For an urgent serving failure before that fix is available, a maintainer\nmay rebuild a known-good `main` revision and push its root deployment commit using an exact lease.\nDo not restore the obsolete Docusaurus tree as the normal rollback path."},"424":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-31","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#risks-and-reviewer-focus","content":"The destructive branch rewrite and public-domain update are high-risk external effects. Reviewers\nmust check the source revision, branch lease, exact CNAME bytes, root-commit parent count, static\ntree inventory, custom-domain response, and whether repository Pages settings still publish\n`gh-pages` from `/`."},"425":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-32","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#risks-and-reviewer-focus","content":"Content risks are stale source mapping, English fallback presented as Chinese, broken generated\nlinks, and unsupported compatibility claims. The automated inventory, localized link checks,\nstatic search checks, browser E2E, and support-policy language reduce those risks; maintainers still\nown technical translation review."},"426":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website-33","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/documentation-website#verification","content":"After an authorized deployment, verify `origin/gh-pages` has no parent, contains the exact CNAME,\nand `https://fronts.js.org/en/docs/` exposes the `main` source revision. The deployment script\nperforms those remote and online checks; a maintainer must review repository Pages settings and the\npublic rendering after the first rollout."},"427":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","type":"page","content":"Releasing Fronts","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Operate and release","Operate and release"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing"},"428":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-0","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","content":"Changesets, local and CI verification, npm trusted publishing bootstrap, prerelease, and stable-release gates."},"429":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-1","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#add-a-change","content":"Add a change"},"430":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-2","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#local-release-verification","content":"Local release verification"},"431":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-3","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"Automated flow"},"432":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-4","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#leaving-prerelease-mode","content":"Leaving prerelease mode"},"433":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-5","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#verification","content":"Verification"},"434":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-6","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","content":"Fronts publishes four public packages with synchronized versions:"},"435":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-7","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","content":"`@fronts/core`"},"436":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-8","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","content":"`@fronts/mf`"},"437":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-9","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","content":"`@fronts/react`"},"438":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-10","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","content":"`@fronts/vue3`"},"439":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-11","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","content":"The repository is currently in Changesets prerelease mode with npm tag `next`."},"440":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-12","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#add-a-change","content":"Every user-visible package change needs a changeset:"},"441":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-13","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#add-a-change","content":"Choose the affected packages and semantic impact. Because the packages are a fixed group,\nChangesets keeps their public versions synchronized while the protocol is stabilizing."},"442":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-14","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#local-release-verification","content":"`pnpm check` performs formatting/lint, a topological clean build, tarball consumption checks,\nTypeScript checks, all unit/integration tests, and enforced coverage thresholds."},"443":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-15","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#local-release-verification","content":"`pnpm verify:packages` packs each public workspace, rejects missing README/LICENSE/dist or leaked\nsource/test directories, installs the four tarballs in an isolated temporary consumer, and imports\nevery public entry through both ESM and CommonJS."},"444":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-16","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#local-release-verification","content":"The development-server E2E run catches local composition regressions. The production-preview run\nperforms a fresh build and is the release gate used by CI; it also exercises producer output that is\nonly available after bundling."},"445":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-17","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"Pushes to `master` run the Changesets action. It either:"},"446":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-18","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"opens/updates a release PR containing version and changelog changes; or"},"447":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-19","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"after that PR is merged, runs `pnpm release` and publishes pending packages."},"448":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-20","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"The GitHub environment should be configured as an npm trusted publisher for this repository and\nthe exact `release.yml` workflow filename. The workflow uses Node 24, upgrades npm to a version\nwith OIDC support, grants `id-token: write`, disables the release dependency cache, and requests\nnpm provenance."},"449":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-21","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"Trusted publishing can only be configured after a package exists. Before the first release:"},"450":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-22","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"confirm the publisher owns the npm `@fronts` scope;"},"451":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-23","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"enable and test GitHub Private Vulnerability Reporting as required by\n`SECURITY.md`;"},"452":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-24","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"add a short-lived granular npm token as the `NPM_TOKEN` repository secret;"},"453":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-25","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"publish the first prerelease through the protected workflow;"},"454":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-26","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"configure all four packages to trust `unadlib/fronts` + `release.yml` for `npm publish`;"},"455":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-27","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"delete the `NPM_TOKEN` secret and revoke the bootstrap token."},"456":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-28","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"After bootstrap, the empty token environment values fall through to npm's short-lived OIDC\ncredential. Do not retain a long-lived publish token as a permanent fallback."},"457":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-29","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#automated-flow","content":"Protect `master` so the Node 22/24 checks and Chromium E2E job are required before merging the\nrelease PR."},"458":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-30","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#leaving-prerelease-mode","content":"After the protocol has met the stable compatibility criteria:"},"459":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-31","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#leaving-prerelease-mode","content":"Review the resulting stable versions and changelogs in a pull request. Do not publish `latest`\nuntil compatibility, security, browser, package-consumer, and rollback gates have passed on the final\ncandidate."},"460":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-32","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#verification","content":"`pnpm check` runs the required non-browser release gate, including isolated packed-package\nconsumption through ESM and CommonJS."},"461":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-33","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#verification","content":"`pnpm test:e2e` and `pnpm test:e2e:preview` verify development composition and fresh production\nartifacts."},"462":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-34","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#verification","content":"`ci.yml` and `release.yml` are the\nautomation sources of truth."},"463":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing-35","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/releasing#verification","content":"Support policy and `SECURITY.md` identify commitments that\nstill require maintainer acceptance or external repository configuration before stable release."},"464":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"page","content":"Runtime Operations","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Operate and release","Operate and release"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations"},"465":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-0","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","content":"Observability, failure handling, replacement, timeouts, testing evidence, and incident correlation for Fronts Hosts."},"466":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-1","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Observability model"},"467":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-2","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#subscribing","content":"Subscribing"},"468":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-3","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#recommended-metrics","content":"Recommended metrics"},"469":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-4","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#failure-semantics","content":"Failure semantics"},"470":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-5","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#audit-and-shutdown","content":"Audit and shutdown"},"471":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-6","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"Replacement runbook"},"472":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-7","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#timeouts","content":"Timeouts"},"473":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-8","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#testing-strategy","content":"Testing strategy"},"474":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-9","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#incident-correlation","content":"Incident correlation"},"475":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-10","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#verification","content":"Verification"},"476":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-11","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Every host has a `hostId`; every application has an `instanceId` and `traceId`. All host events\ncarry a monotonic sequence number, timestamp, and current snapshot. State events additionally carry\nthe duration of the previous state; error events carry a stable Fronts error code and phase."},"477":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-12","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Every `resolve`, `load`, `preload`, `mount`, and `replace` action has one logical operation. Each\nextension receives an immutable context carrying the same `operationId`, `hostId`, `traceId`,\nintent, cancellation signal, and—when an application instance exists—trusted identity. Callers may\nsupply `operationId`/`traceId`, or let the host create them."},"478":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-13","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"For mount and replace, the resolver sees the host-issued identity before a deployment version is\nknown. After resolution, later contexts contain a new frozen identity and operation envelope\nenriched with that version. Extensions must correlate contexts by their IDs, not by object\nreference."},"479":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-14","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Core snapshots and freezes host-owned references, operation contexts, identities, resolution\npolicy, and resolved deployment envelopes. Opaque transport source objects, application props,\nservices, abort signals, and DOM targets retain their domain-specific ownership. Mount captures\nthe props and target references plus either a frozen static container request or a container\nresolver reference before asynchronous resolution. A dynamic container resolver runs after the\ndeployment is resolved and before loader selection; its result is immediately snapshotted.\nBuilt-in `attributes` and iframe `sandbox` collections are copied as part of either request\nsnapshot."},"480":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-15","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Runtime IDs are trimmed and must be non-empty strings. Invalid identifiers are rejected before\nresolution with the error code and phase of the requested operation; custom ID factories are\nvalidated by the same rules."},"481":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-16","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"The intent is one of `resolve`, `load`, `preload`, `mount`, or `replace`. Resolve/load/preload are\nnot application instances, so their operation context deliberately has no `identity`; mount and\nreplace contexts have a required identity and trace. Resolver policy fields remain in\n`ResolveContext`, while its `operation` property carries correlation data. `AppLoader` receives the\noperation context directly, and `ContainerPrepareContext.operation` is the application-scoped\nvariant. Container planning and preparation also receive the frozen `ResolvedApp`, so deployment\nmetadata can choose an execution boundary without a second resolution. This composition keeps\nphase-specific inputs separate without losing end-to-end correlation."},"482":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-17","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Treat identity in these contexts as host-issued authority. Do not accept an application-supplied\nidentity for capability authorization or audit attribution. `operationId` identifies one host\naction; `traceId` may intentionally link several actions, such as preload followed by mount."},"483":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-18","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"The public `FrontsPhase` values are deliberately application-oriented:"},"484":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-19","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"resolve"},"485":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-20","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"load"},"486":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-21","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"container"},"487":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-22","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"mount"},"488":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-23","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"ready"},"489":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-24","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"update"},"490":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-25","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"activate"},"491":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-26","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"deactivate"},"492":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-27","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"unmount"},"493":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-28","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Protocol validation is attributed to the load or mount boundary that encountered it. Replacement\nis a transaction composed from these phases, while audit is a synchronous report rather than an\nerror phase."},"494":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-29","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#observability-model","content":"Module Federation runtime hooks provide lower-level manifest, remote entry, expose, shared, and\nresource events. Correlate the two streams at the `@fronts/mf` load boundary; do not duplicate all\nMF hook payloads into core. The official runtime hooks\nand DevTools loading trace remain the source of truth for MF internals."},"495":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-30","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#subscribing","content":"Provide an initial observer or subscribe later:"},"496":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-31","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-o