ions-78","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#audit-and-shutdown","content":"Direct `resolve()`, `load()`, and `preload()` calls are pending host operations too. They participate\nin the audit count and are aborted when the host is disposed, even though they do not create an\napplication instance."},"544":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-79","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#audit-and-shutdown","content":"Use `host.assertIdle()` after tests, route teardown, or shell shutdown. A failure is evidence of an\napplication/container lifecycle leak and should fail CI."},"545":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-80","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#audit-and-shutdown","content":"`dispose()` aborts direct operations, aborts/unmounts instances, waits for replacement transactions\nand their cleanup, and releases host resources. It rejects with `FRONTS_RUNTIME_LEAK` if cleanup\nfailed or an owned container remains attached; inspect `audit().cleanupFailures` and\n`audit().retainedContainers` for the affected identities. Transport-specific objects with their own\nlifetime should also be disposed by the composition root."},"546":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-81","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"Confirm registry response and immutable artifact availability for old and new deployment."},"547":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-82","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"Preload the target when useful; do not treat preload success as application readiness."},"548":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-83","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"Call `replace()` with a fresh resolution context and stable product trace."},"549":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-84","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"Alert on staging resolve/load/mount/ready failure; the old instance should remain active."},"550":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-85","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"If commit succeeds with `previousCleanupError`, serve the new instance but investigate the leak."},"551":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-86","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"Confirm audit has no retained old container after cleanup."},"552":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-87","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#replacement-runbook","content":"If product validation fails after readiness, point the registry channel back and replace again;\nFronts cannot infer business correctness from render readiness."},"553":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-88","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations#timeouts","content":"Timeout values must be finite and non-negative; `0` disables the corresponding deadline while\n`AbortSignal` cancellation remains active."},"554":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations-89","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/runtime-operations","tags":[],"t