 Until a maintainer\nenables it, the repository has no verified private technical intake channel. A reporter may open a\npublic issue containing only “Private security contact requested” and no vulnerability details,\nproof of concept, affected URL, secret, or exploit information. Wait for a maintainer to establish a\nprivate channel before sharing technical content."},"591":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/security-19","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Enabling GitHub Private Vulnerability Reporting and validating this workflow are release blockers\nfor the first public Fronts 2.0 package."},"592":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/security-20","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/security#what-to-include-privately","content":"Provide enough information to reproduce and assess the issue without including unrelated user or\ntenant data:"},"593":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/security-21","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/security#what-to-include-privately","content":"affected Fronts package, version/commit, entry point, and runtime mode;"},"594":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/security-22","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/security#what-to-include-privately","content":"Host, producer, browser, framework, MF runtime, and producer plugin versions where relevant;"},"595":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/security-23","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/security#what-to-include-privately","content":"security boundary crossed and realistic impact;"},"596":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/security-24","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/security#what-to-include-privately","content":"minimal reproduction or proof of concept;"},