,"url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"Producer mount/readiness failed or exceeded its deadline. Inspect framework errors and readiness settlement."},"920":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-76","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"`FRONTS_LIFECYCLE_FAILED`, `FRONTS_INVALID_STATE`"},"921":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-77","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"A mounted handle failed or the operation is invalid in its current state."},"922":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-78","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"`FRONTS_DUPLICATE_INSTANCE`, `FRONTS_INSTANCE_NOT_FOUND`"},"923":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-79","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"Caller instance ownership is inconsistent. Inspect ID creation and stale handles."},"924":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-80","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"`FRONTS_ABORTED`, `FRONTS_HOST_DISPOSED`"},"925":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-81","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"Navigation/owner cancellation or use after terminal Host disposal. Inspect the signal owner and shutdown order."},"926":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-82","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"`FRONTS_RPC_TIMEOUT`, `FRONTS_RPC_CLOSED`"},"927":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-83","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"Iframe agent or service lifecycle request did not complete on an open channel."},"928":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-84","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"`FRONTS_RUNTIME_LEAK`"},"929":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-85","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"Audit proves active work, cleanup failure, replacement, or retained owned DOM after expected shutdown."},"930":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-86","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#error-categories","content":"Use `frontsErrorCodes` from the package rather than duplicating string literals in application\ncontrol flow."},"931":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-87","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"Check in this order:"},"932":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-88","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"Validate `AppRef.name`, `expose`, `range`, and `channel`; fields must be own, correctly typed\nvalues and identifiers must be non-empty."},"933":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-89","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"Confirm environment, tenant, cohort, and metadata came from a trusted shell policy source."},"934":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-90","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"Confirm the resolver returned the same normalized `ref`, a valid source, and optional non-empty\nversion."},"935":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-91","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"Inspect whether caller cancellation or Host disposal aborted the registry request."},"936":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-92","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"For cached/fallback resolvers, record whether the result came from primary, cache, or fallback\npolicy; do not silently turn an authorization failure into a stale cache hit."},"937":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-93","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"Reproduce resolution without loading code:"},"938":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-94","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#resolution-failures","content":"If this fails, MF, containers, service providers, and producer code are not yet involved."},"939":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-95","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#manifest-or-entry-cannot-be-fetched","content":"Open the exact manifest or remote entry URL from the same browser context."},"940":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-96","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#manifest-or-entry-cannot-be-fetched","content":"Check HTTP status, redirects, CORS, MIME type, TLS, CSP, and final public asset base."},"941":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-97","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#manifest-or-entry-cannot-be-fetched","content":"For a manifest, confirm the response is an MF manifest rather than an HTML fallback, gateway error,\nor unrelated JSON payload."},"942":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-98","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#manifest-or-entry-cannot-be-fetched","content":"Confirm every referenced entry/chunk URL is reachable from the Host—or from the iframe agent when\nisolation is selected."},"943":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-99","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#manifest-or-entry-cannot-be-fetched","content":"Compare development and production-preview output; a dev server success does not prove built asset\npaths."},"944":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-100","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-loads-with-the-wrong-format","content":"An ESM raw entry must be registered with the compatible runtime entry type, such as\n`type: 'module'`."},"945":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-101","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-loads-with-the-wrong-format","content":"A global-format entry needs the producer's expected global/container name."},"946":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-102","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-loads-with-the-wrong-format","content":"Prefer an MF manifest when the producer emits one; it preserves official runtime metadata and\navoids manually duplicating entry details."},"947":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-103","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-loads-with-the-wrong-format","content":"OriginJS in this repository is only a production ESM fixture. Its `dev` command builds and previews\nthe remote; it is not a bundleless remote dev claim."},"948":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-104","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-or-expose-is-not-found","content":"Compare `ModuleFederationSource.remote.name`/`alias` with the runtime registration."},"949":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-105","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-or-expose-is-not-found","content":"Compare `AppRef.expose` with the producer's exposed key, including case and `./` normalization."},"950":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-106","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-or-expose-is-not-found","content":"Confirm the Host passed the intended official MF runtime instance to `@fronts/mf`."},"951":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-107","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-or-expose-is-not-found","content":"Inspect official runtime hooks or DevTools to separate registration, manifest, entry, expose, and\nshared-dependency failures."},"952":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-108","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-name-is-already-bound","content":"`@fronts/mf` rejects silently reusing one remote name for another source or resolved version on the\nsame runtime instance. Use immutable deployment-specific names. Do not enable `force` merely to make\nthe error disappear: official force replacement clears loaded-module caches and changes the shared\nruntime state."},"953":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-109","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#remote-name-is-already-bound","content":"Use force only as an explicit deployment operation with rollback and concurrency review."},"954":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-110","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#shared-dependency-fails","content":"Fronts does not select MF shared versions. Inspect producer/Host share scopes, package names,\nversions, singleton/eager settings, and whether a fallback was emitted. A plugin-free runtime Host\ndoes not automatically provide the build-time share graph of a Vite producer."},"955":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-111","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#shared-dependency-fails","content":"The OriginJS fixture intentionally keeps its generated `@fronts/core` fallback. The official and\nunscoped Vite fixtures bundle the small Fronts protocol instead of relying on a Host share."},"956":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-112","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"The requested expose must default-export an object created by `defineApp()`, `defineReactApp()`, or\n`defineVueApp()`:"},"957":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-113","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"Common failures:"},"958":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-114","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"exporting a React/Vue component instead of a Fronts application;"},"959":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-115","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"exposing a named export while the remote module default is unrelated;"},"960":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-116","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"returning no handle or a handle without `unmount()`;"},"961":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-117","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"hand-constructing an object that lacks the current protocol brand/version;"},"962":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-118","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"wrapping the module so the application is under `default.default`."},"963":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-119","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#invalid-application-exports","content":"Use `host.load()` to isolate resolver/loader/protocol validation from container and mount behavior."},"964":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-120","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"For DOM, Shadow DOM, and custom containers:"},"965":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-121","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"confirm the planned request has a registered, non-empty own `type`;"},"966":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-122","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"validate registry metadata before returning a dynamic container request;"},"967":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-123","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"confirm the Host target belongs to a live document and accepts the new element;"},"968":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-124","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"custom adapters must return matching `type`, an element, a valid mount target, and `dispose()`;"},"969":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-125","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"if `ownsElement` is true, disposal must detach it even after partial failure;"},"970":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-126","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"never mutate a request or resolved envelope after passing it to the Host."},"971":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-127","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#container-failures","content":"If a custom adapter returns an invalid prepared object, Fronts attempts rollback. Inspect the error\ncause for both validation and cleanup failures."},"972":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-128","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"For `FRONTS_CAPABILITY_DENIED`:"},"973":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-129","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"inspect the producer's declared capability names;"},"974":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-130","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"verify the service exists as an own key in static or provider services;"},"975":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-131","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"inspect `capabilityPolicy` with the Host-issued identity;"},"976":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-132","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"inspect whether `createServices` returned a valid service object before cancellation;"},"977":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-133","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"for iframe, compare proxy maximum, parent-authorized scope, and child declaration."},"978":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-134","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"Provider services override same-named static services for one instance. If a provider allocates a\nspan, subscription, channel, or tenant client, its disposer must tolerate partial mount rollback and\nrun exactly once."},"979":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-135","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#capability-and-service-failures","content":"Do not “fix” a denial by exposing all services. Add the narrow capability, policy decision, argument\nvalidation, and audit attribution the application actually needs."},"980":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-136","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#mount-and-readiness-failures","content":"Differentiate mount from readiness:"},"981":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-137","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#mount-and-readiness-failures","content":"`mount` failure means service setup, producer `mount()`, handle validation, or immediate framework\nsetup failed;"},"982":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-138","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#mount-and-readiness-failures","content":"`ready` failure means the returned handle did not become ready, rejected, timed out, or was\ncancelled after mount."},"983":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-139","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#mount-and-readiness-failures","content":"Check framework error boundaries/handlers and the original render exception. A producer readiness\npromise must resolve after the framework commits usable UI, not merely after scheduling a render.\nEvery mount path must return an `unmount()` implementation even when update/activation are omitted."},"984":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-140","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#mount-and-readiness-failures","content":"A timeout should trigger rollback. Increasing the timeout is appropriate only when measured startup\nSLOs justify it; it does not repair a readiness promise that never settles."},"985":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-141","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"`update()` is optional in the producer contract, but calling it when absent intentionally fails."},"986":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-142","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"Updates and activate/deactivate calls are serialized; inspect the prior operation before assuming\na race in the Host."},"987":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-143","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"Do not call lifecycle methods after unmount, abort, failure, or Host disposal."},"988":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-144","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"Use the current live `instanceId`; successful unmount removes it from `host.get()`."},"989":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-145","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"For replacement:"},"990":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-146","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"the current instance must be `ready`, `active`, or `inactive`;"},"991":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-147","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"only one replacement may target it at a time;"},"992":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-148","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"a staging failure leaves the current instance in place;"},"993":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-149","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"`previousCleanupError` means the new instance committed successfully but the previous instance\nleaked or failed unmount—serve the new instance and investigate cleanup;"},"994":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-150","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#lifecycle-and-replacement-failures","content":"if product validation fails after readiness, move the registry/channel decision back and perform\nanother replacement rather than overwriting an already loaded MF registration."},"995":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-151","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#frame-never-connects","content":"`src` and `targetOrigin` must resolve to the same exact, canonical child origin."},"996":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-152","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#frame-never-connects","content":"The child origin must differ from the shell origin."},"997":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-153","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#frame-never-connects","content":"The sandbox must include `allow-scripts` and `allow-same-origin`."},"998":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-154","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#frame-never-connects","content":"The shell must provide `crypto.randomUUID()`."},"999":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-155","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#frame-never-connects","content":"Child `allowedOrigins` must contain the exact shell origin; `*` is rejected."},"1000":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-156","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#frame-never-connects","content":"Confirm the agent bundle ran before the frame `load` event completed and no CSP error blocked it."},"1001":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-157","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#frame-never-connects","content":"Confirm shell `frame-src`, child `frame-ancestors`, script/connect CSP, and artifact CORS."},"1002":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-158","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#handshake-or-rpc-times-out","content":"Compare Host readiness, proxy handshake, parent request, and child request deadlines."},"1003":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-159","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting#handshake-or-rpc-times-out","content":"Inspect whether the child loader fetched the resolved artifact and whether the real app reported\nreadiness."},"1004":{"id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting-160","page_id":"/en/docs/operations/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","