peration contexts for resolvers, loaders, and containers"},"1065":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/core-13","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/core#public-surfaces","content":"typed errors, lifecycle events, replacement, and leak audit"},"1066":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/core-14","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/core#public-surfaces","content":"Additional entry points:"},"1067":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/core-15","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/core#public-surfaces","content":"`@fronts/core/iframe` — origin-bound iframe container/proxy, child agent, and negotiated RPC\ncapabilities"},"1068":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/core-16","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/core#public-surfaces","content":"See the Host Runtime API guide for resolution, preload, mount,\nreplacement, contextual services, observability, and shutdown workflows.\nSee the iframe deployment guide for cross-origin parent/child\nwiring, capability negotiation, browser policy, and production teardown."},"1069":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/core-17","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/core#public-surfaces","content":"The core package has no React, Vue, bundler, or Module Federation dependency. Pair it with\n`@fronts/mf`, a custom loader, or both."},"1070":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/core-18","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/core#public-surfaces","content":"Fronts is currently alpha. Protocol and API changes may occur before 2.0 stable."},"1071":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/core-19","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/core#public-surfaces","content":"MIT"},"1072":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","type":"page","content":"@fronts/mf","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Packages","Packages"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/mf"},"1073":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-0","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/mf","content":"Adapter from resolved Fronts applications to an explicit official Module Federation Runtime instance."},"1074":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-1","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/mf#create-the-adapter","content":"Create the adapter"},"1075":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-2","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/mf#remote-binding-rules","content":"Remote binding rules"},"1076":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-3","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/mf#lifecycle-ownership","content":"Lifecycle ownership"},"1077":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-4","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/mf","content":"`@fronts/mf` is the Module Federation 2 transport adapter for Fronts applications."},"1078":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-5","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/mf","content":"`@module-federation/runtime` is a peer dependency. Supply an explicit official runtime instance;\nthe adapter does not create or discover a global default instance. Fronts is currently alpha, so\nprotocol and API changes may occur before 2.0 stable."},"1079":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-6","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/mf#create-the-adapter","content":"For each resolved application, the adapter uses only public instance methods:\n`registerRemotes()`, `preloadRemote()`, and `loadRemote()`. It does not parse manifests, select\nshared dependencies, modify snapshots, or import `@module-federation/runtime-core`; those remain\nofficial Module Federation responsibilities."},"1080":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-7","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/mf#remote-binding-rules","content":"The official runtime keeps the first registration when a remote name is registered again without\n`force`. The adapter therefore rejects a different source or known resolved version previously\nregistered through Fronts on the same runtime instance. Prefer an immutable, deployment-specific\nremote name. Use force only when intentionally replacing runtime cache; normal rollout should use\nregistry promotion and a Fronts replacement transaction."},"1081":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-8","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/mf#remote-binding-rules","content":"The remote module must default-export a valid `FrontsApp`, normally from an expose named\n`./application`. A component or Bridge application alone does not automatically satisfy the Fronts\nABI. See the Module Federation integration matrix for the\nverified producer boundary."},"1082":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/mf-9","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/mf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/mf#lifecycle-ownership","content":"The resolver chooses a concrete source, this adapter performs transport loading, and the Host owns\nvalidation, service scope, container preparation, readiness, and cleanup. An explicit runtime\ninstance lets the composition root control plugins, share scopes, and transport lifetime without\naccidentally sharing hidden process-wide state. After disposing the Fronts Host, dispose any\nruntime plugin or external-client resources separately owned by that composition root."},"1083":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","type":"page","content":"@fronts/react","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Packages","Packages"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/react"},"1084":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-0","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react","content":"React producer and Host adapters for the framework-neutral Fronts application contract."},"1085":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-1","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/react#producer","content":"Producer"},"1086":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-2","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/react#react-host","content":"React host"},"1087":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-3","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react","content":"React producer and host adapters for the Fronts 2.0 application protocol."},"1088":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-4","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react#producer","content":"`defineReactApp()` owns the React root, commit-based readiness, prop updates, context, error\nboundary, optional Strict Mode, and unmount. A render error rejects the current lifecycle operation\nand shows the configured fallback; a later update remounts the boundary so a valid render can\nrecover. Expose the returned application as a Module Federation module or load it through another\nFronts loader."},"1089":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-5","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react#react-host","content":"The package also exports `useRemoteApp()` for headless integration and hooks for application\nidentity, abort signal, and scoped host services."},"1090":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-6","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react#react-host","content":"The `container` option accepts either a static container request or an async resolver that can\nderive the request from the resolved deployment before Fronts selects its loader."},"1091":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-7","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react#react-host","content":"This adapter is for applications participating in the Fronts host ABI. If an MF-only React\narchitecture only needs framework/router integration, evaluate the official\n`@module-federation/bridge-react` package first."},"1092":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-8","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react#react-host","content":"Fronts is currently alpha. Protocol and API changes may occur before 2.0 stable."},"1093":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/react-9","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/react#react-host","content":"MIT"},"1094":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","type":"page","content":"@fronts/vue3","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Packages","Packages"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3"},"1095":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-0","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","content":"Vue 3 producer and Host adapters for the framework-neutral Fronts application contract."},"1096":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-1","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#producer","content":"Producer"},"1097":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-2","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#vue-host","content":"Vue host"},"1098":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-3","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","content":"Vue 3 producer and host adapters for the Fronts 2.0 application protocol."},"1099":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-4","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#producer","content":"`defineVueApp()` owns the Vue app, provided Fronts context, reactive prop updates, `nextTick()`\nreadiness, optional application configuration, and unmount. It supports Element and ShadowRoot\ntargets."},"1100":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-5","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#vue-host","content":"Use the `RemoteApp` component or `useRemoteApp()` composable with a Fronts host. The package also\nexports composables for application identity, abort signal, and scoped host services."},"1101":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-6","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#vue-host","content":"The `container` prop accepts either a static container request or an async resolver that can derive\nthe request from the resolved deployment before Fronts selects its loader."},"1102":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-7","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#vue-host","content":"This adapter is for applications participating in the Fronts host ABI. If an MF-only Vue\narchitecture only needs framework/router integration, evaluate the official\n`@module-federation/bridge-vue3` package first."},"1103":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-8","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#vue-host","content":"Fronts is currently alpha. Protocol and API changes may occur before 2.0 stable."},"1104":{"id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3-9","page_id":"/en/docs/packages/vue3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/packages/vue3#vue-host","content":"MIT"},"1105":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"page","content":"Host Runtime API","breadcrumbs":["Fronts 2.0 Documentation","Runtime guides","Runtime guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api"},"1106":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-0","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","content":"Operational guide to composing a Fronts Host and using its resolution, loading, lifecycle, replacement, and shutdown APIs."},"1107":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-1","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#purpose","content":"Purpose"},"1108":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-2","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"Composition boundary"},"1109":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-3","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#host-configuration-map","content":"Host configuration map"},"1110":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-4","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#operation-map","content":"Operation map"},"1111":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-5","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#resolution-loading-and-preloading","content":"Resolution, loading, and preloading"},"1112":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-6","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#resolve","content":"`resolve()`"},"1113":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-7","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#load","content":"`load()`"},"1114":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-8","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#preload","content":"`preload()`"},"1115":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-9","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#the-mount-transaction","content":"The mount transaction"},"1116":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-10","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#resolution-aware-container-planning","content":"Resolution-aware container planning"},"1117":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-11","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#contextual-services","content":"Contextual services"},"1118":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-12","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#mounted-application-controls","content":"Mounted application controls"},"1119":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-13","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#readiness-gated-replacement","content":"Readiness-gated replacement"},"1120":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-14","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#observability-and-inspection","content":"Observability and inspection"},"1121":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-15","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#cancellation-and-errors","content":"Cancellation and errors"},"1122":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-16","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#shutdown","content":"Shutdown"},"1123":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-17","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#verification","content":"Verification"},"1124":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-18","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#related-documentation","content":"Related documentation"},"1125":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-19","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#purpose","content":"The Host is the single transaction boundary for resolving, loading, authorizing, mounting, replacing,\nand cleaning up applications. This guide explains when to use each public operation and the\ninvariants callers must preserve. TypeScript declarations in\n`host/types.ts` remain the source of truth for signatures."},"1126":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-20","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#purpose","content":"Use the same Host path for a platform shell, local producer development, Storybook, or integration\ntests. A standalone application needs a static resolver and a local loader; it does not need a\nseparate lifecycle API or global registration mechanism. See the core-only example."},"1127":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-21","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"The composition root owns the Host, resolver, transport loader, container adapters, static services,\nand transport-specific runtime objects. Applications receive only a prepared mount target and their\nauthorized service facade."},"1128":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-22","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"Required boundaries:"},"1129":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-23","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"The resolver chooses a deployment; it MUST NOT load or mount application code."},"1130":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-24","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"The loader returns a module containing a valid `FrontsApp`; it MUST NOT own application lifecycle."},"1131":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-25","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"A container owns its execution surface and MUST remove resources it reports as owned."},"1132":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-26","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"The Host owns transaction ordering, cancellation, readiness, rollback, and audit."},"1133":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-27","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#composition-boundary","content":"A shell MUST dispose transport objects it created in addition to disposing the Fronts Host."},"1134":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-28","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#host-configuration-map","content":"Option group"},"1135":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-29","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#host-configuration-map","content":"Responsibility"},"1136":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-30","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#host-configuration-map","content":"`resolver`, `loader`"},"1137":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-31","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#host-configuration-map","content":"Required deployment-policy and transport boundaries."},"1138":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api-32","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/host-runtime-api#host-configurat