ocs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#lifecycle-and-shutdown","content":"the parent requests child lifecycle unmount;"},"1343":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-84","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#lifecycle-and-shutdown","content":"the child aborts its session and cleans the real app handle;"},"1344":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-85","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#lifecycle-and-shutdown","content":"the child removes its agent root and closes the RPC peer;"},"1345":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-86","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#lifecycle-and-shutdown","content":"the parent closes its peer and the Host revokes the instance service scope;"},"1346":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-87","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#lifecycle-and-shutdown","content":"the iframe container removes the owned element."},"1347":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-88","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#lifecycle-and-shutdown","content":"The parent composition root MUST call `host.dispose()`. The child shell MUST call `agent.stop()` when\nit owns a longer-lived agent lifecycle. `agent.stop()` is idempotent, stops every active session, and\nreports an aggregate lifecycle failure if any child application cannot clean up."},"1348":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-89","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#lifecycle-and-shutdown","content":"The exported `IframeRpcPeer` is a low-level protocol primitive used by the built-in proxy and agent.\nApplication teams SHOULD use the Host service facade instead of registering custom RPC methods or\nmanually constructing connect messages."},"1349":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-90","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#production-checklist","content":"The agent uses a dedicated origin different from every embedding shell origin."},"1350":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-91","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#production-checklist","content":"The shell runs in a context that provides `crypto.randomUUID()` for channel identifiers."},"1351":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-92","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#production-checklist","content":"`src`, `targetOrigin`, and child `allowedOrigins` are exact and environment-specific."},"1352":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-93","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#production-checklist","content":"The frame keeps `allow-scripts` and `allow-same-origin`; every additional token is reviewed."},"1353":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-94","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#production-checklist","content":"Host `frame-src`, child `frame-ancestors`, `script-src`, and `connect-src` are explicit."},"1354":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-95","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment#production-checklist","content":"Remote manifests, entries, chunks, and APIs are HTTPS and CORS-compatible from the child."},"1355":{"id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment-96","page_id":"/en/docs/runtime/iframe-deployment",